BUILD_ONLY: ghcr.io/mll-lab-nu/efe-private:control-transfer-<images/control-transfer/VERSION> (the `-nominal` agent base, the
G1 family's `-train` agent base and the evaluator) is never published (docs/protocol/README.md §1). An evaluation host builds it (images/control-transfer/README.md),
or takes it from the organization's own non-public copy of the package; the roboEngineer Control Transfer tasks reference
that tag and Harbor finds it in the local Docker image store.

Why
  The evaluator stage holds the Neural Fly force surrogate (forces.npz), fitted (by tooling kept outside this repository)
  to the Neural-Fly flight logs (github aerorobotics/neural-fly, pinned commit), whose terms allow personal / educational
  use only and no redistribution. The nominal stage holds only public assets (Unitree mjlab G1 subset: Apache-2.0;
  MuJoCo Menagerie unitree_go2: BSD-3-Clause; skydio_x2: Apache-2.0) and could be public on its own.

What the builder needs
  Network access to github.com (the three pinned upstream checkouts) and PyPI; the preparation runs in a plain
  python:3.12 container (numpy 2.3.1, mujoco 3.5.0, scipy 1.17.0). The fit reproduces the documented validation RMSE;
  its file digest is pinned in each Neural Fly task's environment/sim/scripts/control_transfer/trusted/fly.py ASSET_SHA256
  (the evaluator checks it at start).
